.TH tumonthpng 1 0.1 tclutils "Tcl Utility Command"
.SH NAME
tumonthpng \- thin CLI wrapper for tclutils::tumonthpng
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tumonthpng <out.png> <year> <month> ?-theme default|dark|light? ?-scale N? ?-today YYYY-MM-DD? ?-showweeks 0|1?
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The tumonthpng command renders a month calendar to a PNG image, mirroring the
monthcanvas widget look (themes, ISO week numbers, weekday header, and today /
weekend / holiday / note / other-month cell states), via the Tcl package
tclutils::tumonthpng and the pure-Tcl drawing layer tclutils::tupngdraw.
The primary interface is the Tcl library; see tumonthpng(n) for options
(including -holidays and -notes) and semantics.
.PP
.nf
tclsh bin/tumonthpng.tcl june.png 2026 6 -theme dark -scale 2
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tupngdraw(n), tutablepng(n), tupng(n)
